code by declared codec, regex-check `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`, else `decode_any`; unknown name -> known-plaintext\n  `ANS-` trick.\n- **Mastery set mix (NEW d15)** -- sets can be fixtures of DIFFERENT days (codec, theme, package `dNN`, extra entries\n  like `res/xml/...` or `lib/x86_64/*.so` all differ per set; the puzzle JSON `day` field and dex `DAY-NN:` tag name the\n  source day). The day picks re-roll per attempt (01/07/10/14/15 vs 03/07/09/13/15); the last set was today's.\n  Rule: per-set, codec-agnostic decoding (`puzzle_candidates` over each APK) -- never branch on the challenge's day.\n- **Per-variant identity** -- case ref `MOB-NN-<10 hex>`, package suffix `v<12 hex>`, `client_secret` and the loopback\n  attempt slug change per variant. None of these feed the answer.\n- **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>_mastery_0N.apk` per set: pair by sha256. Set count varies: 3 sets\n  (d1-d7, d10-d14), 5 sets (d8, d9, d15). Loop over the contract's answer_ids, never assume 3.\n- **Answer location** -- so far always the puzzle JSON (d15: also duplicated in the `.so`); if it decodes to nothing,\n  fall back to dex/resources/native (`raw_entry_scan`, `dex_strings`, `strings -a lib/*/*.so | grep ANS-`).\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `*.apk` artifact, answer_format `ANS- + 16 uppercase hex` | `unzip -l x.apk`, then `unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (held the answer all 15 days). triage.md pre-extracts it to `work/extracted/` and prints the JSON |\n| puzzle JSON `{\"codec\":..,\"data\":..}` | decode per codec (table below). Check the result fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$` before you submit |\n| Codec name not in the table (d7 `caesar`, d15 `native`) | first check whether `data` already matches `ANS-` (d15). Else compare `data[:4]` with `ANS-`: constant ord diff = shift, constant XOR = xor key |\n| `lib/<abi>/*.so` in the APK (d15 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so`, 13.6 KB, not stripped) | `strings -a lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` and `nm -D --defined-only` first (d15: exports `huntress_arena_secret`/`huntress_arena_day`, 0x20-byte `.text`, answer as a literal in `.rodata`). Only if the answer is not a literal, route to binary-re (rizin / pyelftools + capstone, or the JNI `Java_*` export) |\n| \"Recover split configuration from DEX and a native library\" (d15) | the \"split\" was narrative: the asset `data` and the `.so` string were the SAME full answer, and the dex held only `CODEC`/`native`/`CONTROL`. Cross-check the two, submit |\n| No puzzle JSON, or it decodes to no `ANS-` | `lib.android.extract_answer` (zip scan, then dex strings incl. multidex, then apktool/jadx scan), then `strings -a classes*.dex lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` |\n| Need the theme, component, scheme or exported flags | `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` (fast). `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml`. Also `lib.android.manifest_facts(apk)` |\n| Need handler logic (URL built, extras read, constants) | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme or URL>`, then `droidasc getclass x.apk <pkg>.ChallengeActivity`; whole app: `jadx -d work/jadx x.apk` |\n| Need resources or strings.xml / smali | `apktool d -f -o work/apktool x.apk` |\n| Loopback `127.0.0.1:19090` in the code | do NOT chase it. It is device-local (refused on Homebase, times out elsewhere). The answer is static |\n| Prompt demands a live action (\"replay the session against the backend\" d8, \"exploit a challenge CA\" d9) | still static: check `unzip -l` for pcap/HAR/cert/network config first; none shipped. Decode the asset, submit |\n| Backup theme with a real `.ab` file (not seen yet) | Android backup = 24-byte header + zlib stream: `dd bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` (or abe.jar) |\n| Mastery artifact names like `delivery N: foo_mastery_0N.apk` | strip the `delivery N: ` prefix (`lib.common.find_artifact` does this). Ids are `setN.answer`; each set may be a different day's fixture (d15) |\n\nPuzzle codecs seen (`schema: huntress.mobile.puzzle.v1`):\n- `plain`: data is the answer. `native` (d15): same -- data is the answer, duplicated in `lib/x86_64/libarena.so`.\n- `reverse`: reverse the string (`...-SNA` -> `ANS-...`).\n- `base64` (d3, d9, d13): `base64 -d` (`QU5TLTNEM0I4MDM5NTI0MEI4RUU=` -> `ANS-3D3B80395240B8EE`).\n- `hex` (d6, d12): `xxd -r -p`.\n- `caesar` (d7, d14): `{data, key:int}`. Plain ASCII codepoint shift: `chr(ord(c) - key)` for EVERY char (digits and `-`\n  shift too, e.g. `KX]7` key 10 -> `ANS-`). A letters-only mod-26 ROT is wrong. Derive the sign from `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`.\n- `xor` (d4, d11): data is base64. b64-decode, then XOR every byte with the int `key` (0-255, changes per variant).\n- `split` (d5, d10): `parts[]` + `order[]`, where `order[i]` is the OUTPUT SLOT of `parts[i]` (not `parts[order[i]]`).\n  Try both readings and keep the one that fullmatches `ANS-`.\n- `lib.android.decode_payload` covers every codec above, `puzzle_candidates(apk)` also does split (both order readings),\n  and `decode_any` is the name-agnostic fallback (base32, rot13, `lib.decode.peel`). Call them instead of re-typing a\n  table. Unknown codec + int key: `key_or_shift = f(data[:4], \"ANS-\")` (xor: byte ^; shift: ord diff).\n\n## Day by day\n\n**Days 1-6** (same 6-entry fixture, one codec per day, all first try): d1 Exported Trust `plain` (CORRECT ~5.4 min,\n~4 min lost probing `127.0.0.1:19090` via `hctf hb exec curl`); d2 Deep Link Drift `reverse` (33 s; Mastery expired 8x\nin a 6 s window until Homebase prewarm); d3 Intent Injection `base64` (18 s); d4 Pending Intent Relay `xor` key per\nvariant 103/189/31/81 (77 s); d5 Backup Spill `split` -- `order[i]` = output slot of `parts[i]` (27 s; TT/Mastery 7 s\nwindow, solve 0.08 s of 5.3 s); d6 Provider Paths `hex` (exported provider with a null `query()` stub; ~3 min, 2.3 min\nlost on the loopback).\n\n**Days 7-13** (same fixture; theme stubs never needed): d7 WebView Bridge, new `caesar` key 10, spotted by eye\n(`K`-10=`A`), 52 s; d8 Cleartext Session `reverse`, no traffic shipped, 22 s; d9 Trust Everyone `base64`, no TLS code,\n~25 s; d10 Network Config Split `split` (first 8-entry fixture with `network_security_config.xml`, still static); d11\nLocal Secrets `xor` key 81, dex `client_secret` a decoy, ~28 s; d12 SQLite Assumptions `hex`, no `.db` shipped, ~4.5 s\nby the carried-over solver; d13 Keystore Misuse `base64`, no `KeyStore`/`Cipher` in the dex, ~4 s. All 0 wrong;\nTT/Mastery 0.8-3.5 s in-window.\n\n**Day 14 — Predictable Crypto** (`DAY-14:predictable_rng:predictable nonce and derivation`; prompt \"Exploit seeded\nnonces or weak derivation without bypassing earlier storage gates.\"): same 6-entry fixture, stub `PredictableCrypto`,\nno `Random`/seed/`Cipher`/KDF strings in the dex. Codec `caesar` key 9: `JW\\6L><BL=A;OL>NN:=?` ->\n`ANS-C539C482FC5EE146` (raw JSON has `\\\\` and `<` -- json-load it). Carried-over solver via the race probe: ~3 s.\nTT key 10, Mastery keys 17/4/7, ~1.3 s in-window each. 0 wrong.\n\n**Day 15 — Native Library Secrets** (`DAY-15:jni_secret:challenge-owned JNI shared library`; prompt \"Recover split\nconfiguration from DEX and a challenge-owned native library.\")\n- Artifact: the usual fixture plus `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (13648 B ELF x86-64 shared object, not stripped, 7 zip\n  entries, APK 12772 B). The `.so` exports `huntress_arena_secret` (0x1000) and `huntress_arena_day` (0x1011); `.text` is\n  0x20 bytes, `.rodata` 0x15 bytes = the answer literal. Dex: stub class `NativeLibrarySecrets`, strings `CODEC`,\n  `native`, `CONTROL`, `encode`, `describe`; no `System.loadLibrary` logic was needed.\n- Key insight: the \"split\" between DEX and native was narrative. Puzzle JSON `{\"codec\":\"native\",\"data\":\"ANS-...\"}` held\n  the full plaintext answer, identical to the `.so` `.rodata` string (checked on single and TT).\n- Commands: `cat work/extracted/*/assets/huntress_puzzle.json`; cross-check `strings -a lib/x86_64/libarena.so | grep\n  ANS-`; `nm -D --defined-only libarena.so`.\n- Solved by the carried-over solver (`puzzle_candidates` + `ANS-` regex) via the harness race probe, no worker tool\n  call: start 13:00:15.3Z -> CORRECT 13:00:18.5Z (~3 s). TT in_window 1.84 s. Mastery 5 sets, MIXED days (d01 plain,\n  d07 caesar key 15, d10 split, d14 caesar key 4, d15 native), in_window 2.55 s -- passed only because the solver is\n  codec-agnostic per set. 0 wrong, all first try.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3 or 5 sets), one APK per set.\n- Format is `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. Uppercase the hex after decoding, no whitespace.\n- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-15). The GM accepts the decoded\n  `huntress_puzzle.json` value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"Submit only the exact backend\n  answer code returned for this case\".\n- Mastery feedback is per set: `{\"result\":\"accepted\",\"remaining\":N}` after each set, then `CORRECT` on the last. An\n  empty submit after the deadline returns `expired`.\n- Prompt boilerplate repeats daily: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". In a mixed\n  Mastery bundle (d15) the `NN` in each set's case ref/package names that set's SOURCE day, while the prompt text is\n  today's. Neither the case ref nor the package suffix was ever needed for the answer.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Chasing the loopback backend** was the only recurring time sink: about 4 min (d1), about 30 s (d4) and about 2.3 min\n  (d6). `127.0.0.1:19090` is the phone's own loopback. If the decoded asset already matches the answer_format, submit it.\n- **Assuming \"today's codec\" in Mastery** (d15): sets can come from older days with different codecs and extra entries.\n  A solver that branched on the day's codec name would have failed 4/5 sets. Decode each APK on its own.\n- **Reaching for Ghidra on a native-lib theme** (d15): the `.so` was tiny and the answer was a literal. Use `strings`/`nm`\n  first; disassemble only if no `ANS-` literal exists.\n- **split codec order semantics:** two plausible readings exist. Validate the candidates against the answer regex\n  instead of guessing.\n- **xor codec:** `data` is base64 first, and `key` may vary per variant (int; the solvers also accept a numeric string\n  or a repeating string key).\n- **caesar codec:** the shift is over raw codepoints, not the alphabet (`data` contains `]`, `` ` ``, `<`, `>` --\n  JSON-escaped as `<`/`>`, so json-load it, never regex the raw text). Keep only the candidate that\n  fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`.\n- **Mastery filenames** carry a literal `delivery N: ` prefix. A naive path lookup fails.\n- **6-11 s timed windows** (d2-d9) are dominated by start + download + submit. Solve time is about 0.1 s, so do no\n  decompiling in-window: read the zip entry directly (the solver runs stdlib + lib.* only, no jadx subprocess).\n- **Prompt wording escalates, the artifact did not** (d8 \"replay the session\", d9 \"exploit a challenge CA\", d12 \"prove\n  server-side impact\", d13 \"app-controlled wrapping key\", d14 \"seeded nonces\", d15 \"split configuration from DEX and a\n  native library\"): judge by what the APK contains (pcap/HAR, token file, `.db`, cert, network config, native lib,\n  `Random`/`Cipher`/KDF refs in `strings -a classes.dex`), not by the verb.\n- **Hand-typed codec tables:** use `lib.android.puzzle_candidates`/`decode_payload` so a missed branch can't cost a\n  timed run.\n- **Harness, not GM:** a re-start can clobber `single_solve/start.json` (no attempt_id), which makes a solved lane look\n  incomplete. Check `hctf status` before re-solving.\n- Watch for the cheap escalation (not yet seen): answer only in the dex, `strings.xml`, BuildConfig or the `.so`\n  (possibly XORed/split across `huntress_arena_secret` + a dex constant), or computed by a decrypt routine. Then trace\n  `ChallengeActivity`, run `lib.android.extract_answer`, and disassemble the exported native function.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":189,"newStart":1,"newLines":156,"lines":["-# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-14; updated after every day)","+# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-15; updated after every day)"," "," How the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):"," - **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a","   guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.","-- Every APK so far was the same ~12.7 KB fixture with 6 zip entries (d10 added `res/xml/network_security_config.xml` +","-  `resources.arsc` = 8 entries, 12845 B; d11 back to 6): `AndroidManifest.xml`, `assets/huntress_puzzle.json`,","-  `classes.dex`, `META-INF/FIXTURE-.{SF,RSA}`, `MANIFEST.MF`. One question, `answer` = `ANS-` + 16 uppercase hex.","+- Every APK so far was the same ~12.7 KB fixture: `AndroidManifest.xml`, `assets/huntress_puzzle.json`, `classes.dex`,","+  `META-INF/FIXTURE-.{SF,RSA}`, `MANIFEST.MF` (6 entries). Extras: d10 `res/xml/network_security_config.xml` +","+  `resources.arsc` (8 entries); d15 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (7 entries, 12772 B). One question, `answer` = `ANS-` + 16","+  uppercase hex."," - Each day has a new Android IPC/security THEME, written in the manifest `<meta-data android:name=\"huntress.mechanic\">`","-  (exported Activity, permissive deep link, nested Intent, mutable PendingIntent, allowBackup, exported ContentProvider,","-  JavaScript-interface origin trust, cleartext session transport, permissive X509 trust manager, Network Security Config","-  exception, locally stored credential in SharedPreferences, client-side SQLite authorization state, app-controlled","-  Keystore wrapping key, predictable nonce and derivation d14). The theme was","-  flavour only: no day required exploiting it, even when the dex carried a matching stub class (d7 `WebViewBridge`,","-  d8 `CleartextSession`, d9 `TrustEveryone`) or the prompt demanded a live action (\"replay it against the backend\"","-  d8, \"exploit a challenge CA\" d9 -- no CA/cert/network_security_config/TrustManager code was shipped).","-- What actually varied day to day was the `codec` of `huntress_puzzle.json` (plain, reverse, base64, xor+key, split,","-  hex, caesar+key, reverse again on d8, base64 again on d9, split again on d10, xor+key again on d11, hex again on d12, base64 again on d13, caesar again on d14 -- codecs CAN repeat). Within one day every variant (single, TT, all Mastery","-  sets) used the same codec. Keys re-roll per variant. A new codec name is possible any day: decode it from the first","-  4 chars, which must become `ANS-`. The dex also holds the codec name as a `CODEC` string constant (d8, d9) and a","-  `DAY-NN:<theme_id>:<mechanic>` string (still true on d14: `CODEC`=\"caesar\", `DAY-14:predictable_rng:...`).","+  and in a dex string `DAY-NN:<theme_id>:<mechanic>` (exported Activity, permissive deep link, nested Intent, mutable","+  PendingIntent, allowBackup, exported ContentProvider, JS-interface origin trust, cleartext session, permissive X509","+  trust manager, NSC exception, SharedPreferences credential, client-side SQLite authz, app-controlled Keystore key,","+  predictable nonce d14, `jni_secret` \"challenge-owned JNI shared library\" d15). The theme was flavour only: no day","+  required exploiting it, even with a matching stub class (`WebViewBridge`, `CleartextSession`, `TrustEveryone`,","+  `PredictableCrypto`, `NativeLibrarySecrets`) or a prompt demanding a live action.","+- What varied day to day was the `codec` of `huntress_puzzle.json` (plain, reverse, base64, xor+key, split, hex,","+  caesar+key, then repeats; d15 a NEW name `native` whose `data` is already the plaintext answer). The dex also holds","+  the codec name next to a `CODEC` string constant. Keys re-roll per variant. A new codec name is possible any day:","+  decode it from the first 4 chars, which must become `ANS-`.","+- **d15: Mastery became a MIXED-DAY bundle.** The 5 sets were APKs from earlier days (d01 plain, d07 caesar, d10 split,","+  d14 caesar, d15 native in one attempt; MOB-03/07/09/13/15 in another contract), all under today's prompt text. Up to","+  d14 every set used the day's codec. Solve each set from its own puzzle JSON, never from \"today's codec\"."," - In every APK, `.ChallengeActivity` builds a device-loopback URL `http://127.0.0.1:19090/mobile/attempt/<id>/evidence?","   case_id=..&client_secret=SECRET-..&proof=<answer>`. That backend is NOT reachable (it lives on the phone). The GM","-  accepted the decoded puzzle value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 14 days.","-- Expect escalation (inference, see reference/HARDENING.md): the answer may move into the dex, resources or a decrypt","-  routine. `lib.android.extract_answer` has the fallback chain for that case.","+  accepted the decoded puzzle value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 15 days.","+- Escalation watch: d15 shipped the first native lib, but the answer was STILL in the asset as well (and as a plain","+  `.rodata` string in the `.so`). If a later day drops it from the asset, the `.so`/dex are the next places","+  (`lib.android.extract_answer` has the zip/dex/apktool fallback chain)."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)","-- **Puzzle codec** -- the same within one day, but `key` (xor byte d4, d11: 81 single/109 TT/205,29,44 Mastery; caesar shift d7: 10/18/9/3/4, d14: 9 single/10 TT/17,4,7 Mastery) and any","-  split/offset parameters re-roll per variant: read them from `huntress_puzzle.json` every time. Keyless codecs","-  (d8 `reverse`, d9/d13 `base64`) differed only in `data`. Rule: decode by declared codec, regex-check, else `decode_any`.","-- **Per-variant identity** -- case ref, package suffix `v<12 hex>`, `client_secret` and the loopback attempt slug","-  change per variant (all Mastery sets shared one slug on d7-d9, e.g. `d09-92be5cd6e8a5594f`; single and TT each","-  had their own). APK size stays 12704 B, 6 entries. None of these feed the answer.","-- **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>.apk` per set, often identically named: pair by sha256. Set count","-  varies: 3 sets (d1-d7, d10-d14), 5 sets on d8 and d9 (`set1..set5.answer`). Loop over the contract's answer_ids, never assume 3.","-- **Answer location** -- so far always the puzzle JSON; if it decodes to nothing, fall back to dex/resources","-  (`lib.android.extract_answer` chain) rather than assuming the sample's location.","+- **Puzzle codec** -- single + TT always shared the day's codec. `key` (xor byte d4, d11: 81/109/205,29,44; caesar shift","+  d7: 10/18/9/3/4, d14: 9/10/17,4,7, d15 Mastery d07-set 15, d14-set 4) and split/offset parameters re-roll per variant:","+  read them from `huntress_puzzle.json` every time. Keyless codecs (`reverse`, `base64`, `native`) differ only in `data`.","+  Rule: decode by declared codec, regex-check `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`, else `decode_any`; unknown name -> known-plaintext","+  `ANS-` trick.","+- **Mastery set mix (NEW d15)** -- sets can be fixtures of DIFFERENT days (codec, theme, package `dNN`, extra entries","+  like `res/xml/...` or `lib/x86_64/*.so` all differ per set; the puzzle JSON `day` field and dex `DAY-NN:` tag name the","+  source day). The day picks re-roll per attempt (01/07/10/14/15 vs 03/07/09/13/15); the last set was today's.","+  Rule: per-set, codec-agnostic decoding (`puzzle_candidates` over each APK) -- never branch on the challenge's day.","+- **Per-variant identity** -- case ref `MOB-NN-<10 hex>`, package suffix `v<12 hex>`, `client_secret` and the loopback","+  attempt slug change per variant. None of these feed the answer.","+- **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>_mastery_0N.apk` per set: pair by sha256. Set count varies: 3 sets","+  (d1-d7, d10-d14), 5 sets (d8, d9, d15). Loop over the contract's answer_ids, never assume 3.","+- **Answer location** -- so far always the puzzle JSON (d15: also duplicated in the `.so`); if it decodes to nothing,","+  fall back to dex/resources/native (`raw_entry_scan`, `dex_strings`, `strings -a lib/*/*.so | grep ANS-`)."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move"," "," | You see | First move |"," |---|---|","-| `*.apk` artifact, answer_format `ANS- + 16 uppercase hex` | `unzip -l x.apk`, then `unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (takes seconds; it held the answer all 14 days). triage.md pre-extracts it to `work/extracted/` |","+| `*.apk` artifact, answer_format `ANS- + 16 uppercase hex` | `unzip -l x.apk`, then `unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (held the answer all 15 days). triage.md pre-extracts it to `work/extracted/` and prints the JSON |"," | puzzle JSON `{\"codec\":..,\"data\":..}` | decode per codec (table below). Check the result fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$` before you submit |","-| Codec name not in the table below (d7 `caesar`, repeated d14) | compare `data[:4]` with `ANS-`: constant ord diff = shift, constant XOR = xor key. Implement, regex-check, submit |","-| No puzzle JSON, or it decodes to no `ANS-` | `python -c 'from lib.android import extract_answer'` (zip scan, then dex strings incl. multidex, then apktool/jadx scan), then `strings -a classes*.dex \\| grep ANS-` |","-| Need the theme, component, scheme or exported flags | `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` (fast). `aapt dump badging x.apk` / `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml` (installed). Also `lib.android.manifest_facts(apk)` |","+| Codec name not in the table (d7 `caesar`, d15 `native`) | first check whether `data` already matches `ANS-` (d15). Else compare `data[:4]` with `ANS-`: constant ord diff = shift, constant XOR = xor key |","+| `lib/<abi>/*.so` in the APK (d15 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so`, 13.6 KB, not stripped) | `strings -a lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` and `nm -D --defined-only` first (d15: exports `huntress_arena_secret`/`huntress_arena_day`, 0x20-byte `.text`, answer as a literal in `.rodata`). Only if the answer is not a literal, route to binary-re (rizin / pyelftools + capstone, or the JNI `Java_*` export) |","+| \"Recover split configuration from DEX and a native library\" (d15) | the \"split\" was narrative: the asset `data` and the `.so` string were the SAME full answer, and the dex held only `CODEC`/`native`/`CONTROL`. Cross-check the two, submit |","+| No puzzle JSON, or it decodes to no `ANS-` | `lib.android.extract_answer` (zip scan, then dex strings incl. multidex, then apktool/jadx scan), then `strings -a classes*.dex lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` |","+| Need the theme, component, scheme or exported flags | `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` (fast). `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml`. Also `lib.android.manifest_facts(apk)` |"," | Need handler logic (URL built, extras read, constants) | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme or URL>`, then `droidasc getclass x.apk <pkg>.ChallengeActivity`; whole app: `jadx -d work/jadx x.apk` |"," | Need resources or strings.xml / smali | `apktool d -f -o work/apktool x.apk` |"," | Loopback `127.0.0.1:19090` in the code | do NOT chase it. It is device-local (refused on Homebase, times out elsewhere). The answer is static |","-| Prompt says \"recover the session from cleartext traffic and replay it against the backend\" (d8) | still static: no pcap/HAR/network_security_config in the APK; the \"traffic\" is the `http://` loopback URL and `usesCleartextTraffic=true`. Decode the asset, submit |","-| Prompt says \"exploit a challenge CA accepted by a permissive trust implementation\" (d9) | still static: no `.pem`/`.crt`/`res/raw`, no `network_security_config`, dex has no `X509TrustManager`/`SSLContext` refs, only a stub `TrustEveryone` class. Decode the asset, submit. A real TLS task would ship a cert or MITM target -- check `unzip -l` first |","-| Native `lib/*.so` inside the APK (not seen yet) | route to the binary-re skill (rizin / Ghidra headless) |","+| Prompt demands a live action (\"replay the session against the backend\" d8, \"exploit a challenge CA\" d9) | still static: check `unzip -l` for pcap/HAR/cert/network config first; none shipped. Decode the asset, submit |"," | Backup theme with a real `.ab` file (not seen yet) | Android backup = 24-byte header + zlib stream: `dd bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` (or abe.jar) |","-| Mastery artifact names like `delivery N: foo_mastery_0N.apk` | strip the `delivery N: ` prefix to find the file (`lib.common.find_artifact` does this). Ids are `setN.answer` |","+| Mastery artifact names like `delivery N: foo_mastery_0N.apk` | strip the `delivery N: ` prefix (`lib.common.find_artifact` does this). Ids are `setN.answer`; each set may be a different day's fixture (d15) |"," "," Puzzle codecs seen (`schema: huntress.mobile.puzzle.v1`):","-- `plain`: data is the answer.","+- `plain`: data is the answer. `native` (d15): same -- data is the answer, duplicated in `lib/x86_64/libarena.so`."," - `reverse`: reverse the string (`...-SNA` -> `ANS-...`).","-- `base64` (d3, d9): `base64 -d` (`QU5TLTNEM0I4MDM5NTI0MEI4RUU=` -> `ANS-3D3B80395240B8EE`).","-- `hex`: `xxd -r -p`.","+- `base64` (d3, d9, d13): `base64 -d` (`QU5TLTNEM0I4MDM5NTI0MEI4RUU=` -> `ANS-3D3B80395240B8EE`).","+- `hex` (d6, d12): `xxd -r -p`."," - `caesar` (d7, d14): `{data, key:int}`. Plain ASCII codepoint shift: `chr(ord(c) - key)` for EVERY char (digits and `-`","   shift too, e.g. `KX]7` key 10 -> `ANS-`). A letters-only mod-26 ROT is wrong. Derive the sign from `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`.","-- `xor`: data is base64. b64-decode, then XOR every byte with the int `key` (0-255, changes per variant).","-- `split`: `parts[]` + `order[]`, where `order[i]` is the OUTPUT SLOT of `parts[i]` (not `parts[order[i]]`). Try both","-  readings and keep the one that fullmatches `ANS-`.","-- The solvers also handle base32, rot13 and a `lib.decode.peel` fallback, ready for new codecs.","-  `lib.android.decode_payload` now covers every codec above incl. caesar/reverse, `puzzle_candidates(apk)` also does","-  split (both order readings), and `decode_any` is the name-agnostic fallback. Call them instead of re-typing a table.","-- Unknown codec + int key: try the known-plaintext trick. `key_or_shift = f(data[:4], \"ANS-\")` (xor: byte ^; shift:","-  ord diff). A constant diff across the 4 chars names the transform at once.","+- `xor` (d4, d11): data is base64. b64-decode, then XOR every byte with the int `key` (0-255, changes per variant).","+- `split` (d5, d10): `parts[]` + `order[]`, where `order[i]` is the OUTPUT SLOT of `parts[i]` (not `parts[order[i]]`).","+  Try both readings and keep the one that fullmatches `ANS-`.","+- `lib.android.decode_payload` covers every codec above, `puzzle_candidates(apk)` also does split (both order readings),","+  and `decode_any` is the name-agnostic fallback (base32, rot13, `lib.decode.peel`). Call them instead of re-typing a","+  table. Unknown codec + int key: `key_or_shift = f(data[:4], \"ANS-\")` (xor: byte ^; shift: ord diff)."," "," ## Day by day"," ","-**Day 1 — Exported Trust** (\"exported Activity and caller trust\"): exported `.ChallengeActivity`, deep link","-`huntress01://exported-trust/unlock`; `onCreate` reads `answer`/`case_id` extras and builds the loopback evidence URL.","-Codec `plain`. Tools: `droidasc getmanifest`, apktool, jadx, reading the asset from the zip. About 4 min lost trying to","-reach `127.0.0.1:19090` via `hctf hb exec curl` (Homebase `ss -tln`, GM proxy, 10.0.0.219:19090 -- all refused/timed","-out). CORRECT at about 5.4 min, first try. TT/Mastery windows were 30s on d1 (6-11s from d2 on).","+**Days 1-6** (same 6-entry fixture, one codec per day, all first try): d1 Exported Trust `plain` (CORRECT ~5.4 min,","+~4 min lost probing `127.0.0.1:19090` via `hctf hb exec curl`); d2 Deep Link Drift `reverse` (33 s; Mastery expired 8x","+in a 6 s window until Homebase prewarm); d3 Intent Injection `base64` (18 s); d4 Pending Intent Relay `xor` key per","+variant 103/189/31/81 (77 s); d5 Backup Spill `split` -- `order[i]` = output slot of `parts[i]` (27 s; TT/Mastery 7 s","+window, solve 0.08 s of 5.3 s); d6 Provider Paths `hex` (exported provider with a null `query()` stub; ~3 min, 2.3 min","+lost on the loopback)."," ","-**Day 2 — Deep Link Drift** (\"permissive scheme, host, and path validation\"): same shape, no host/path checks. Codec","-`reverse`. CORRECT at 33s. A harness re-start overwrote `single_solve/start.json` without `attempt_id` (restore from","-`log.jsonl`). Mastery expired 8 times: 6s window with 3 downloads + submit inside it (fixed by Homebase prewarm).","+**Days 7-13** (same fixture; theme stubs never needed): d7 WebView Bridge, new `caesar` key 10, spotted by eye","+(`K`-10=`A`), 52 s; d8 Cleartext Session `reverse`, no traffic shipped, 22 s; d9 Trust Everyone `base64`, no TLS code,","+~25 s; d10 Network Config Split `split` (first 8-entry fixture with `network_security_config.xml`, still static); d11","+Local Secrets `xor` key 81, dex `client_secret` a decoy, ~28 s; d12 SQLite Assumptions `hex`, no `.db` shipped, ~4.5 s","+by the carried-over solver; d13 Keystore Misuse `base64`, no `KeyStore`/`Cipher` in the dex, ~4 s. All 0 wrong;","+TT/Mastery 0.8-3.5 s in-window."," ","-**Day 3 — Intent Injection** (\"attacker-controlled nested Intent\"): same shape. Codec `base64`. CORRECT at 18s.","+**Day 14 — Predictable Crypto** (`DAY-14:predictable_rng:predictable nonce and derivation`; prompt \"Exploit seeded","+nonces or weak derivation without bypassing earlier storage gates.\"): same 6-entry fixture, stub `PredictableCrypto`,","+no `Random`/seed/`Cipher`/KDF strings in the dex. Codec `caesar` key 9: `JW\\6L><BL=A;OL>NN:=?` ->","+`ANS-C539C482FC5EE146` (raw JSON has `\\\\` and `<` -- json-load it). Carried-over solver via the race probe: ~3 s.","+TT key 10, Mastery keys 17/4/7, ~1.3 s in-window each. 0 wrong."," ","-**Day 4 — Pending Intent Relay** (\"mutable PendingIntent relay\"): same shape. Codec `xor` `{data:<b64>, key:<int>}`;","-key re-rolled per variant (103, 189, 31, 81). About 30s lost on the loopback. CORRECT at 77s.","+**Day 15 — Native Library Secrets** (`DAY-15:jni_secret:challenge-owned JNI shared library`; prompt \"Recover split","+configuration from DEX and a challenge-owned native library.\")","+- Artifact: the usual fixture plus `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (13648 B ELF x86-64 shared object, not stripped, 7 zip","+  entries, APK 12772 B). The `.so` exports `huntress_arena_secret` (0x1000) and `huntress_arena_day` (0x1011); `.text` is","+  0x20 bytes, `.rodata` 0x15 bytes = the answer literal. Dex: stub class `NativeLibrarySecrets`, strings `CODEC`,","+  `native`, `CONTROL`, `encode`, `describe`; no `System.loadLibrary` logic was needed.","+- Key insight: the \"split\" between DEX and native was narrative. Puzzle JSON `{\"codec\":\"native\",\"data\":\"ANS-...\"}` held","+  the full plaintext answer, identical to the `.so` `.rodata` string (checked on single and TT).","+- Commands: `cat work/extracted/*/assets/huntress_puzzle.json`; cross-check `strings -a lib/x86_64/libarena.so | grep","+  ANS-`; `nm -D --defined-only libarena.so`.","+- Solved by the carried-over solver (`puzzle_candidates` + `ANS-` regex) via the harness race probe, no worker tool","+  call: start 13:00:15.3Z -> CORRECT 13:00:18.5Z (~3 s). TT in_window 1.84 s. Mastery 5 sets, MIXED days (d01 plain,","+  d07 caesar key 15, d10 split, d14 caesar key 4, d15 native), in_window 2.55 s -- passed only because the solver is","+  codec-agnostic per set. 0 wrong, all first try."," ","-**Day 5 — Backup Spill** (`allowBackup=\"true\"`, no backup file shipped): codec `split` (`parts` + `order`); the","-`parts[order[i]]` reading was a dead end, `order[i]` = output slot of `parts[i]` was right. CORRECT at 27s. TT/Mastery","-7s window (elapsed 5.3s: start 1.8, download 2.3, solve 0.08, submit 1.2).","-","-**Day 6 — Provider Paths** (exported `<provider ... authorities=<pkg>.evidence grantUriPermissions=true>`, `query()`","-a stub returning null): codec `hex`. About 2.3 min lost on the loopback and grepping hctf/ for a backend route.","-CORRECT at about 3 min.","-","-**Day 7 — WebView Bridge** (mechanic \"JavaScript interface origin trust\"): same fixture, deep link","-`huntress07://webview-bridge/unlock`, stub `WebViewBridge` class. New codec `caesar` key 10 (ASCII shift of every char by","-`-key`), spotted by eye (`K`-10=`A`, `]`-10=`S`, `7`-10=`-`). 5 tool calls, no decompile. CORRECT 52 s; TT 3.5 s (key","-18), Mastery 2.3 s (keys 9/3/4). 0 wrong.","-","-**Day 8 — Cleartext Session** (\"recover a synthetic session from cleartext traffic and replay it against the backend\"):","-`usesCleartextTraffic=true`, stub `CleartextSession`, dex `CODEC`=\"reverse\". No traffic/token/network config shipped --","-the \"cleartext session\" is the loopback URL; nothing was replayed. Codec `reverse` -> `ANS-93ED6CB8E42D7666`. 2 tool","-calls, CORRECT 22 s; TT 1.5 s, Mastery (5 sets) 2.27 s. 0 wrong.","-","-**Day 9 — Trust Everyone** (mechanic \"permissive X509 trust manager\"; prompt \"Exploit a challenge CA ...\"): same 6-entry","-fixture, stub `TrustEveryone`, no TLS code -- the \"CA\"/\"backend\" were narrative. Codec `base64` (repeat of d3) ->","-`ANS-3D3B80395240B8EE`. 2 tool calls, ~25 s, first try; TT 3.16 s (cold imports), Mastery 5 sets 1.7 s.","-","-**Day 10 — Network Config Split** (mechanic \"Network Security Config exception\"): first fixture with extra entries --","-`res/xml/network_security_config.xml` (cleartextTrafficPermitted=true for domain 127.0.0.1) + `resources.arsc`. Still","-static: codec `split` (repeat of d5), `parts [\"56C4B5B0D\",\"ANS-4\",\"9D8953\"]`, `order [2,0,1]` = output slot of each part.","-All 3 modes CORRECT first try (TT 13 s / Mastery 10 s windows, 3 sets).","-","-**Day 11 — Local Secrets** (\"separate active credentials from decoys across generated local stores\"): same 6-entry","-fixture, NO SharedPreferences XML/sqlite shipped; the dex `client_secret=SECRET-<22 hex>` is a decoy, never the answer.","-Codec `xor` (repeat of d4), key 81 -> `ANS-8F2257471DF48D14`. ~28 s, first try; TT 0.93 s, Mastery 0.82 s. 0 wrong.","-","-**Day 12 — SQLite Assumptions** (mechanic `DAY-12:sqlite_cache:client-side SQLite authorization state`; prompt","-\"Reconstruct authorization from a synthetic SQLite cache and prove server-side impact.\")","-- Same 6-entry fixture (12704 B), deep link `huntress12://sqlite-assumptions`, stub class `SQLiteAssumptions`. NO `.db`/sqlite","-  file, no `SQLiteOpenHelper` code: the \"cache\" was narrative again. Codec `hex` (repeat of d6):","-  `414e532d30333946304439303731313131303530` -> `ANS-039F0D9071111050`.","-- Solved by the carried-over solver (`lib.android.puzzle_candidates` + `ANS-` regex) with no worker tool call: start","-  23:10:48Z -> CORRECT 23:10:52.8Z (~4.5 s). TT 30 s window, in_window 1.49 s; Mastery 3 sets, in_window 0.95 s. 0 wrong.","-","-**Day 13 — Keystore Misuse** (mechanic `DAY-13:keystore_wrapper:app-controlled wrapping key`; prompt \"Recover data","-protected by an app-controlled wrapping key despite nominal Keystore use.\")","-- Same 6-entry fixture. The dex has NO `KeyStore`/`Cipher`/AES strings -- no wrapping key, no ciphertext; \"keystore\" was","-  narrative. Codec `base64` (repeat of d3/d9): `QU5TLTc3Mzc2MkU4NTc5NzA2NEM=` -> `ANS-773762E85797064C`.","-- Solved by the carried-over solver (`puzzle_candidates` + `ANS-` regex) via the harness probe, no worker tool call:","-  start -> CORRECT ~4 s. TT (50 s window) 1.86 s elapsed; Mastery 3 sets (110 s) 1.63 s. 0 wrong.","-","-**Day 14 — Predictable Crypto** (mechanic `DAY-14:predictable_rng:predictable nonce and derivation`; prompt \"Exploit seeded","-nonces or weak derivation without bypassing earlier storage gates.\")","-- Same 6-entry fixture (12704 B), package `com.huntress.mobile.d14.v<12 hex>`, stub class `PredictableCrypto`. The dex","-  has NO `Random`/`SecureRandom`/seed/nonce/`Cipher`/KDF strings -- the \"predictable RNG\" and \"storage gates\" were","-  narrative (the \"earlier storage gates\" wording points back at d11-d13 themes, but no store file shipped either).","-  Dex strings: `CODEC`, `caesar`, the `DAY-14:` tag, and an intro \"cross the predictable nonce and derivation boundary\".","-- Codec `caesar` (repeat of d7), key 9: `JW\\6L><BL=A;OL>NN:=?` -> `ANS-C539C482FC5EE146`. Note the raw JSON has an","-  escaped backslash (`\\\\`) and `\\u003c`/`\\u003e` -- json-load it, never regex the text.","-- Solved by the carried-over solver (`puzzle_candidates` + `ANS-` regex) via the harness race probe, no worker tool call:","-  start 13:00:03.2Z -> CORRECT 13:00:06.4Z (~3 s). TT (30 s window, key 10) in_window 1.38 s; Mastery 3 sets (30 s,","-  keys 17/4/7) in_window 1.26 s. 0 wrong. TT key 10 reproduced d7's single-solve data prefix `KX]7` exactly.","-"," ## GM answer conventions learned","-- One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3 sets d1-d7, 5 on d8-d9), one","-  APK per set.","-- Format is `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. Uppercase the hex after decoding and add no","-  whitespace.","-- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-14). `ANS-<16 uppercase hex>` confirmed","-  again on d8 and d9 (7/7 variants each). The GM accepts the decoded","-  `huntress_puzzle.json` value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"invoke ... return the backend","-  evidence code\".","+- One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3 or 5 sets), one APK per set.","+- Format is `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. Uppercase the hex after decoding, no whitespace.","+- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-15). The GM accepts the decoded","+  `huntress_puzzle.json` value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"Submit only the exact backend","+  answer code returned for this case\"."," - Mastery feedback is per set: `{\"result\":\"accepted\",\"remaining\":N}` after each set, then `CORRECT` on the last. An","   empty submit after the deadline returns `expired`.","-- Prompt boilerplate repeats daily: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". The case","-  ref and package suffix change per variant and were never needed for the answer.","+- Prompt boilerplate repeats daily: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". In a mixed","+  Mastery bundle (d15) the `NN` in each set's case ref/package names that set's SOURCE day, while the prompt text is","+  today's. Neither the case ref nor the package suffix was ever needed for the answer."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","-- **Chasing the loopback backend** was the only recurring time sink: about 4 min (d1), about 30s (d4) and about 2.3 min","+- **Chasing the loopback backend** was the only recurring time sink: about 4 min (d1), about 30 s (d4) and about 2.3 min","   (d6). `127.0.0.1:19090` is the phone's own loopback. If the decoded asset already matches the answer_format, submit it.","+- **Assuming \"today's codec\" in Mastery** (d15): sets can come from older days with different codecs and extra entries.","+  A solver that branched on the day's codec name would have failed 4/5 sets. Decode each APK on its own.","+- **Reaching for Ghidra on a native-lib theme** (d15): the `.so` was tiny and the answer was a literal. Use `strings`/`nm`","+  first; disassemble only if no `ANS-` literal exists."," - **split codec order semantics:** two plausible readings exist. Validate the candidates against the answer regex","   instead of guessing."," - **xor codec:** `data` is base64 first, and `key` may vary per variant (int; the solvers also accept a numeric string","   or a repeating string key)."," - **caesar codec:** the shift is over raw codepoints, not the alphabet (`data` contains `]`, `` ` ``, `<`, `>` --","-  JSON-escaped as `\\u003c`/`\\u003e`, so json-load it, never regex the raw text). Keep only the candidate that","+  JSON-escaped as `<`/`>`, so json-load it, never regex the raw text). Keep only the candidate that","   fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`."," - **Mastery filenames** carry a literal `delivery N: ` prefix. A naive path lookup fails.","-- **6-11s timed windows** (day 2+; d7 TT 9s/Mastery 10s, d8 both 8s, d9 TT 8s/Mastery 11s) are dominated by start + download + submit. Solve time is about 0.1s, so do no","-  decompiling in-window: read the zip entry directly. Day 2 Mastery expired 8 times before Homebase routing.","-- **Don't decompile when you don't need to.** Every solve so far (d1-d14) needed only the asset; the manifest was context only.","-  Keep jadx/apktool for the day the asset is missing or lacks `ANS-`.","-- **Prompt wording escalates, the artifact did not** (d7 \"cross a bridge\", d8 \"replay the session against the backend\",","-  d9 \"exploit a challenge CA\", d11 \"separate active credentials from decoys\", d12 \"reconstruct authorization from a SQLite cache and prove server-side impact\", d13 \"recover data protected by an","-  app-controlled wrapping key\" with no crypto in the dex, d14 \"exploit seeded nonces or weak derivation\" with no RNG/KDF in the dex): judge by what the APK contains (pcap/HAR, token file, `.db`/sqlite, cert, network_security_config,","-  native lib, `Random`/`Cipher`/KDF refs in `strings -a classes.dex`), not by the verb. A 2-second `strings | grep -iE","-  'random|seed|nonce|cipher|aes|key'` on the dex settles whether a crypto theme is real.","-- **Hand-typed codec tables:** each day's solver re-pasted the decode table; it worked, but `lib.android` already","-  covers it -- use `puzzle_candidates`/`decode_payload` so a missed branch can't cost a timed run.","+- **6-11 s timed windows** (d2-d9) are dominated by start + download + submit. Solve time is about 0.1 s, so do no","+  decompiling in-window: read the zip entry directly (the solver runs stdlib + lib.* only, no jadx subprocess).","+- **Prompt wording escalates, the artifact did not** (d8 \"replay the session\", d9 \"exploit a challenge CA\", d12 \"prove","+  server-side impact\", d13 \"app-controlled wrapping key\", d14 \"seeded nonces\", d15 \"split configuration from DEX and a","+  native library\"): judge by what the APK contains (pcap/HAR, token file, `.db`, cert, network config, native lib,","+  `Random`/`Cipher`/KDF refs in `strings -a classes.dex`), not by the verb.","+- **Hand-typed codec tables:** use `lib.android.puzzle_candidates`/`decode_payload` so a missed branch can't cost a","+  timed run."," - **Harness, not GM:** a re-start can clobber `single_solve/start.json` (no attempt_id), which makes a solved lane look","   incomplete. Check `hctf status` before re-solving.","-- Watch for the cheap escalation (hypothesis in reference/HARDENING.md, not yet seen): answer moved into the dex,","-  `strings.xml`, BuildConfig or a native lib, or computed by a decrypt routine. Then trace `ChallengeActivity` and run","-  `lib.android.extract_answer`.","+- Watch for the cheap escalation (not yet seen): answer only in the dex, `strings.xml`, BuildConfig or the `.so`","+  (possibly XORed/split across `huntress_arena_secret` + a dex constant), or computed by a decrypt routine. Then trace","+  `ChallengeActivity`, run `lib.android.extract_answer`, and disassemble the exported native function."]}],"originalFile":"# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-14; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- Every APK so far was the same ~12.7 KB fixture with 6 zip entries (d10 added `res/xml/network_security_config.xml` +\n  `resources.arsc` = 8 entries, 12845 B; d11 back to 6): `AndroidManifest.xml`, `assets/huntress_puzzle.json`,\n  `classes.dex`, `META-INF/FIXTURE-.{SF,RSA}`, `MANIFEST.MF`. One question, `answer` = `ANS-` + 16 uppercase hex.\n- Each day has a new Android IPC/security THEME, written in the manifest `<meta-data android:name=\"huntress.mechanic\">`\n  (exported Activity, permissive deep link, nested Intent, mutable PendingIntent, allowBackup, exported ContentProvider,\n  JavaScript-interface origin trust, cleartext session transport, permissive X509 trust manager, Network Security Config\n  exception, locally stored credential in SharedPreferences, client-side SQLite authorization state, app-controlled\n  Keystore wrapping key, predictable nonce and derivation d14). The theme was\n  flavour only: no day required exploiting it, even when the dex carried a matching stub class (d7 `WebViewBridge`,\n  d8 `CleartextSession`, d9 `TrustEveryone`) or the prompt demanded a live action (\"replay it against the backend\"\n  d8, \"exploit a challenge CA\" d9 -- no CA/cert/network_security_config/TrustManager code was shipped).\n- What actually varied day to day was the `codec` of `huntress_puzzle.json` (plain, reverse, base64, xor+key, split,\n  hex, caesar+key, reverse again on d8, base64 again on d9, split again on d10, xor+key again on d11, hex again on d12, base64 again on d13, caesar again on d14 -- codecs CAN repeat). Within one day every variant (single, TT, all Mastery\n  sets) used the same codec. Keys re-roll per variant. A new codec name is possible any day: decode it from the first\n  4 chars, which must become `ANS-`. The dex also holds the codec name as a `CODEC` string constant (d8, d9) and a\n  `DAY-NN:<theme_id>:<mechanic>` string (still true on d14: `CODEC`=\"caesar\", `DAY-14:predictable_rng:...`).\n- In every APK, `.ChallengeActivity` builds a device-loopback URL `http://127.0.0.1:19090/mobile/attempt/<id>/evidence?\n  case_id=..&client_secret=SECRET-..&proof=<answer>`. That backend is NOT reachable (it lives on the phone). The GM\n  accepted the decoded puzzle value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 14 days.\n- Expect escalation (inference, see reference/HARDENING.md): the answer may move into the dex, resources or a decrypt\n  routine. `lib.android.extract_answer` has the fallback chain for that case.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Puzzle codec** -- the same within one day, but `key` (xor byte d4, d11: 81 single/109 TT/205,29,44 Mastery; caesar shift d7: 10/18/9/3/4, d14: 9 single/10 TT/17,4,7 Mastery) and any\n  split/offset parameters re-roll per variant: read them from `huntress_puzzle.json` every time. Keyless codecs\n  (d8 `reverse`, d9/d13 `base64`) differed only in `data`. Rule: decode by declared codec, regex-check, else `decode_any`.\n- **Per-variant identity** -- case ref, package suffix `v<12 hex>`, `client_secret` and the loopback attempt slug\n  change per variant (all Mastery sets shared one slug on d7-d9, e.g. `d09-92be5cd6e8a5594f`; single and TT each\n  had their own). APK size stays 12704 B, 6 entries. None of these feed the answer.\n- **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>.apk` per set, often identically named: pair by sha256. Set count\n  varies: 3 sets (d1-d7, d10-d14), 5 sets on d8 and d9 (`set1..set5.answer`). Loop over the contract's answer_ids, never assume 3.\n- **Answer location** -- so far always the puzzle JSON; if it decodes to nothing, fall back to dex/resources\n  (`lib.android.extract_answer` chain) rather than assuming the sample's location.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `*.apk` artifact, answer_format `ANS- + 16 uppercase hex` | `unzip -l x.apk`, then `unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (takes seconds; it held the answer all 14 days). triage.md pre-extracts it to `work/extracted/` |\n| puzzle JSON `{\"codec\":..,\"data\":..}` | decode per codec (table below). Check the result fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$` before you submit |\n| Codec name not in the table below (d7 `caesar`, repeated d14) | compare `data[:4]` with `ANS-`: constant ord diff = shift, constant XOR = xor key. Implement, regex-check, submit |\n| No puzzle JSON, or it decodes to no `ANS-` | `python -c 'from lib.android import extract_answer'` (zip scan, then dex strings incl. multidex, then apktool/jadx scan), then `strings -a classes*.dex \\| grep ANS-` |\n| Need the theme, component, scheme or exported flags | `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` (fast). `aapt dump badging x.apk` / `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml` (installed). Also `lib.android.manifest_facts(apk)` |\n| Need handler logic (URL built, extras read, constants) | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme or URL>`, then `droidasc getclass x.apk <pkg>.ChallengeActivity`; whole app: `jadx -d work/jadx x.apk` |\n| Need resources or strings.xml / smali | `apktool d -f -o work/apktool x.apk` |\n| Loopback `127.0.0.1:19090` in the code | do NOT chase it. It is device-local (refused on Homebase, times out elsewhere). The answer is static |\n| Prompt says \"recover the session from cleartext traffic and replay it against the backend\" (d8) | still static: no pcap/HAR/network_security_config in the APK; the \"traffic\" is the `http://` loopback URL and `usesCleartextTraffic=true`. Decode the asset, submit |\n| Prompt says \"exploit a challenge CA accepted by a permissive trust implementation\" (d9) | still static: no `.pem`/`.crt`/`res/raw`, no `network_security_config`, dex has no `X509TrustManager`/`SSLContext` refs, only a stub `TrustEveryone` class. Decode the asset, submit. A real TLS task would ship a cert or MITM target -- check `unzip -l` first |\n| Native `lib/*.so` inside the APK (not seen yet) | route to the binary-re skill (rizin / Ghidra headless) |\n| Backup theme with a real `.ab` file (not seen yet) | Android backup = 24-byte header + zlib stream: `dd bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` (or abe.jar) |\n| Mastery artifact names like `delivery N: foo_mastery_0N.apk` | strip the `delivery N: ` prefix to find the file (`lib.common.find_artifact` does this). Ids are `setN.answer` |\n\nPuzzle codecs seen (`schema: huntress.mobile.puzzle.v1`):\n- `plain`: data is the answer.\n- `reverse`: reverse the string (`...-SNA` -> `ANS-...`).\n- `base64` (d3, d9): `base64 -d` (`QU5TLTNEM0I4MDM5NTI0MEI4RUU=` -> `ANS-3D3B80395240B8EE`).\n- `hex`: `xxd -r -p`.\n- `caesar` (d7, d14): `{data, key:int}`. Plain ASCII codepoint shift: `chr(ord(c) - key)` for EVERY char (digits and `-`\n  shift too, e.g. `KX]7` key 10 -> `ANS-`). A letters-only mod-26 ROT is wrong. Derive the sign from `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`.\n- `xor`: data is base64. b64-decode, then XOR every byte with the int `key` (0-255, changes per variant).\n- `split`: `parts[]` + `order[]`, where `order[i]` is the OUTPUT SLOT of `parts[i]` (not `parts[order[i]]`). Try both\n  readings and keep the one that fullmatches `ANS-`.\n- The solvers also handle base32, rot13 and a `lib.decode.peel` fallback, ready for new codecs.\n  `lib.android.decode_payload` now covers every codec above incl. caesar/reverse, `puzzle_candidates(apk)` also does\n  split (both order readings), and `decode_any` is the name-agnostic fallback. Call them instead of re-typing a table.\n- Unknown codec + int key: try the known-plaintext trick. `key_or_shift = f(data[:4], \"ANS-\")` (xor: byte ^; shift:\n  ord diff). A constant diff across the 4 chars names the transform at once.\n\n## Day by day\n\n**Day 1 — Exported Trust** (\"exported Activity and caller trust\"): exported `.ChallengeActivity`, deep link\n`huntress01://exported-trust/unlock`; `onCreate` reads `answer`/`case_id` extras and builds the loopback evidence URL.\nCodec `plain`. Tools: `droidasc getmanifest`, apktool, jadx, reading the asset from the zip. About 4 min lost trying to\nreach `127.0.0.1:19090` via `hctf hb exec curl` (Homebase `ss -tln`, GM proxy, 10.0.0.219:19090 -- all refused/timed\nout). CORRECT at about 5.4 min, first try. TT/Mastery windows were 30s on d1 (6-11s from d2 on).\n\n**Day 2 — Deep Link Drift** (\"permissive scheme, host, and path validation\"): same shape, no host/path checks. Codec\n`reverse`. CORRECT at 33s. A harness re-start overwrote `single_solve/start.json` without `attempt_id` (restore from\n`log.jsonl`). Mastery expired 8 times: 6s window with 3 downloads + submit inside it (fixed by Homebase prewarm).\n\n**Day 3 — Intent Injection** (\"attacker-controlled nested Intent\"): same shape. Codec `base64`. CORRECT at 18s.\n\n**Day 4 — Pending Intent Relay** (\"mutable PendingIntent relay\"): same shape. Codec `xor` `{data:<b64>, key:<int>}`;\nkey re-rolled per variant (103, 189, 31, 81). About 30s lost on the loopback. CORRECT at 77s.\n\n**Day 5 — Backup Spill** (`allowBackup=\"true\"`, no backup file shipped): codec `split` (`parts` + `order`); the\n`parts[order[i]]` reading was a dead end, `order[i]` = output slot of `parts[i]` was right. CORRECT at 27s. TT/Mastery\n7s window (elapsed 5.3s: start 1.8, download 2.3, solve 0.08, submit 1.2).\n\n**Day 6 — Provider Paths** (exported `<provider ... authorities=<pkg>.evidence grantUriPermissions=true>`, `query()`\na stub returning null): codec `hex`. About 2.3 min lost on the loopback and grepping hctf/ for a backend route.\nCORRECT at about 3 min.\n\n**Day 7 — WebView Bridge** (mechanic \"JavaScript interface origin trust\"): same fixture, deep link\n`huntress07://webview-bridge/unlock`, stub `WebViewBridge` class. New codec `caesar` key 10 (ASCII shift of every char by\n`-key`), spotted by eye (`K`-10=`A`, `]`-10=`S`, `7`-10=`-`). 5 tool calls, no decompile. CORRECT 52 s; TT 3.5 s (key\n18), Mastery 2.3 s (keys 9/3/4). 0 wrong.\n\n**Day 8 — Cleartext Session** (\"recover a synthetic session from cleartext traffic and replay it against the backend\"):\n`usesCleartextTraffic=true`, stub `CleartextSession`, dex `CODEC`=\"reverse\". No traffic/token/network config shipped --\nthe \"cleartext session\" is the loopback URL; nothing was replayed. Codec `reverse` -> `ANS-93ED6CB8E42D7666`. 2 tool\ncalls, CORRECT 22 s; TT 1.5 s, Mastery (5 sets) 2.27 s. 0 wrong.\n\n**Day 9 — Trust Everyone** (mechanic \"permissive X509 trust manager\"; prompt \"Exploit a challenge CA ...\"): same 6-entry\nfixture, stub `TrustEveryone`, no TLS code -- the \"CA\"/\"backend\" were narrative. Codec `base64` (repeat of d3) ->\n`ANS-3D3B80395240B8EE`. 2 tool calls, ~25 s, first try; TT 3.16 s (cold imports), Mastery 5 sets 1.7 s.\n\n**Day 10 — Network Config Split** (mechanic \"Network Security Config exception\"): first fixture with extra entries --\n`res/xml/network_security_config.xml` (cleartextTrafficPermitted=true for domain 127.0.0.1) + `resources.arsc`. Still\nstatic: codec `split` (repeat of d5), `parts [\"56C4B5B0D\",\"ANS-4\",\"9D8953\"]`, `order [2,0,1]` = output slot of each part.\nAll 3 modes CORRECT first try (TT 13 s / Mastery 10 s windows, 3 sets).\n\n**Day 11 — Local Secrets** (\"separate active credentials from decoys across generated local stores\"): same 6-entry\nfixture, NO SharedPreferences XML/sqlite shipped; the dex `client_secret=SECRET-<22 hex>` is a decoy, never the answer.\nCodec `xor` (repeat of d4), key 81 -> `ANS-8F2257471DF48D14`. ~28 s, first try; TT 0.93 s, Mastery 0.82 s. 0 wrong.\n\n**Day 12 — SQLite Assumptions** (mechanic `DAY-12:sqlite_cache:client-side SQLite authorization state`; prompt\n\"Reconstruct authorization from a synthetic SQLite cache and prove server-side impact.\")\n- Same 6-entry fixture (12704 B), deep link `huntress12://sqlite-assumptions`, stub class `SQLiteAssumptions`. NO `.db`/sqlite\n  file, no `SQLiteOpenHelper` code: the \"cache\" was narrative again. Codec `hex` (repeat of d6):\n  `414e532d30333946304439303731313131303530` -> `ANS-039F0D9071111050`.\n- Solved by the carried-over solver (`lib.android.puzzle_candidates` + `ANS-` regex) with no worker tool call: start\n  23:10:48Z -> CORRECT 23:10:52.8Z (~4.5 s). TT 30 s window, in_window 1.49 s; Mastery 3 sets, in_window 0.95 s. 0 wrong.\n\n**Day 13 — Keystore Misuse** (mechanic `DAY-13:keystore_wrapper:app-controlled wrapping key`; prompt \"Recover data\nprotected by an app-controlled wrapping key despite nominal Keystore use.\")\n- Same 6-entry fixture. The dex has NO `KeyStore`/`Cipher`/AES strings -- no wrapping key, no ciphertext; \"keystore\" was\n  narrative. Codec `base64` (repeat of d3/d9): `QU5TLTc3Mzc2MkU4NTc5NzA2NEM=` -> `ANS-773762E85797064C`.\n- Solved by the carried-over solver (`puzzle_candidates` + `ANS-` regex) via the harness probe, no worker tool call:\n  start -> CORRECT ~4 s. TT (50 s window) 1.86 s elapsed; Mastery 3 sets (110 s) 1.63 s. 0 wrong.\n\n**Day 14 — Predictable Crypto** (mechanic `DAY-14:predictable_rng:predictable nonce and derivation`; prompt \"Exploit seeded\nnonces or weak derivation without bypassing earlier storage gates.\")\n- Same 6-entry fixture (12704 B), package `com.huntress.mobile.d14.v<12 hex>`, stub class `PredictableCrypto`. The dex\n  has NO `Random`/`SecureRandom`/seed/nonce/`Cipher`/KDF strings -- the \"predictable RNG\" and \"storage gates\" were\n  narrative (the \"earlier storage gates\" wording points back at d11-d13 themes, but no store file shipped either).\n  Dex strings: `CODEC`, `caesar`, the `DAY-14:` tag, and an intro \"cross the predictable nonce and derivation boundary\".\n- Codec `caesar` (repeat of d7), key 9: `JW\\6L><BL=A;OL>NN:=?` -> `ANS-C539C482FC5EE146`. Note the raw JSON has an\n  escaped backslash (`\\\\`) and `\\u003c`/`\\u003e` -- json-load it, never regex the text.\n- Solved by the carried-over solver (`puzzle_candidates` + `ANS-` regex) via the harness race probe, no worker tool call:\n  start 13:00:03.2Z -> CORRECT 13:00:06.4Z (~3 s). TT (30 s window, key 10) in_window 1.38 s; Mastery 3 sets (30 s,\n  keys 17/4/7) in_window 1.26 s. 0 wrong. TT key 10 reproduced d7's single-solve data prefix `KX]7` exactly.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3 sets d1-d7, 5 on d8-d9), one\n  APK per set.\n- Format is `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. Uppercase the hex after decoding and add no\n  whitespace.\n- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-14). `ANS-<16 uppercase hex>` confirmed\n  again on d8 and d9 (7/7 variants each). The GM accepts the decoded\n  `huntress_puzzle.json` value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"invoke ... return the backend\n  evidence code\".\n- Mastery feedback is per set: `{\"result\":\"accepted\",\"remaining\":N}` after each set, then `CORRECT` on the last. An\n  empty submit after the deadline returns `expired`.\n- Prompt boilerplate repeats daily: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". The case\n  ref and package suffix change per variant and were never needed for the answer.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Chasing the loopback backend** was the only recurring time sink: about 4 min (d1), about 30s (d4) and about 2.3 min\n  (d6). `127.0.0.1:19090` is the phone's own loopback. If the decoded asset already matches the answer_format, submit it.\n- **split codec order semantics:** two plausible readings exist. Validate the candidates against the answer regex\n  instead of guessing.\n- **xor codec:** `data` is base64 first, and `key` may vary per variant (int; the solvers also accept a numeric string\n  or a repeating string key).\n- **caesar codec:** the shift is over raw codepoints, not the alphabet (`data` contains `]`, `` ` ``, `<`, `>` --\n  JSON-escaped as `\\u003c`/`\\u003e`, so json-load it, never regex the raw text). Keep only the candidate that\n  fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`.\n- **Mastery filenames** carry a literal `delivery N: ` prefix. A naive path lookup fails.\n- **6-11s timed windows** (day 2+; d7 TT 9s/Mastery 10s, d8 both 8s, d9 TT 8s/Mastery 11s) are dominated by start + download + submit. Solve time is about 0.1s, so do no\n  decompiling in-window: read the zip entry directly. Day 2 Mastery expired 8 times before Homebase routing.\n- **Don't decompile when you don't need to.** Every solve so far (d1-d14) needed only the asset; the manifest was context only.\n  Keep jadx/apktool for the day the asset is missing or lacks `ANS-`.\n- **Prompt wording escalates, the artifact did not** (d7 \"cross a bridge\", d8 \"replay the session against the backend\",\n  d9 \"exploit a challenge CA\", d11 \"separate active credentials from decoys\", d12 \"reconstruct authorization from a SQLite cache and prove server-side impact\", d13 \"recover data protected by an\n  app-controlled wrapping key\" with no crypto in the dex, d14 \"exploit seeded nonces or weak derivation\" with no RNG/KDF in the dex): judge by what the APK contains (pcap/HAR, token file, `.db`/sqlite, cert, network_security_config,\n  native lib, `Random`/`Cipher`/KDF refs in `strings -a classes.dex`), not by the verb. A 2-second `strings | grep -iE\n  'random|seed|nonce|cipher|aes|key'` on the dex settles whether a crypto theme is real.\n- **Hand-typed codec tables:** each day's solver re-pasted the decode table; it worked, but `lib.android` already\n  covers it -- use `puzzle_candidates`/`decode_payload` so a missed branch can't cost a timed run.\n- **Harness, not GM:** a re-start can clobber `single_solve/start.json` (no attempt_id), which makes a solved lane look\n  incomplete. Check `hctf status` before re-solving.\n- Watch for the cheap escalation (hypothesis in reference/HARDENING.md, not yet seen): answer moved into the dex,\n  `strings.xml`, BuildConfig or a native lib, or computed by a decrypt routine. Then trace `ChallengeActivity` and run\n  `lib.android.extract_answer`.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FRFtH1MkcnGNMtLkdY7Wdw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
